<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Looking to use a format similar to those of SCP-4028, SCP-3020 and SCP-3031. Audio files if possible.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A memetic agent starts spreading across finished musical compositions. Depending on the fame, the listener's perception and the themes the peace touches, this agent can cause all sorts of benefitial or detrimental changes on a person's body and psyche. Although the agent starts propagating on niche music spheres, it eventually reaches mainstream hits.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Trough different evidence we learn about our PoI, an anomalous individual who was heavily involved in his country's music scene. In naive attempt to improve his situation and the one of his fellow companions, he ends up risking up the veil and getting the community he so much loved killed (both metaphorically and literally). After barely surviving lynching and escaping persecution, he releases the memetic agent with ambiguous motivations.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Aside from the fact this skip deals with a not so explored topic, this entry has the intent of confronting the Foundation with a fundamental dilemma: is it really better to live on your knees than to die on your feet? Is the Foundation really willing to declare a war on artistic expression for the greater good?.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> It's Intended to be a connection between our PoI and the GoI &quot;Deer College&quot;, this may change in the future.</p>

