														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4836743">
									

<p>I find myself in the same place as Nico here, in that it's a competently written work that isn't quite satisfactory to me, though some of the sentence structuring threw me off a few more times than I would have liked. Obviously, that's a personal gripe, but it is what it is.</p>
<p>It feels like the parts that are stretched are all within setting the atmosphere, which while I appreciate, leaves the last log feeling a bit like retreading ground. I feel like a way to remedy that would be to have introduced -A later than within the initial phases of the description. I think having that come out later would allow for a more natural flow of establishing that the place is real, has a history of abandonment, and a reason to want more people to come through would pull the pieces a little tighter.</p>

							</div>

								
					
