<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A sentient fountain that doesn't want to be played in or climbed on creates hydrophobia-inducing water.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> School-kids on their senior year start spreading a local legend among their younger peers and other people to not to interact with a certain fountain. One day, a pipe of the fountain is burst by the fountain, spreading a town’s water supply, creating a hydrophobic town.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The fountain itself and its experience as a structure that's always been alive for years.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This is an old idea that already has a draft, as it was liked by many reviewers back when it was first made, both in IRC chatrooms and forum posts. (This draft is about 2-3 years old.) I took a long hiatus from skip writing, but I may be returning to finish this skip. I wonder if the idea itself has aged well, but I might as well see if it gets greenlit so I can advance it towards the draft forum and hope to get it published soon. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Despite trying to write skips 2-3 years ago, am I still considered a first-time author?</span></p>

